Z||000000||rnoswal||09-13-2000||10:36 PM||||There are a few postal jeeps in the junkyard around here and I was wondering if anyone knows how I can tell if they are the super duty engines. They had the carbureted intake but the carbs are gone. They are 4 cylinder and look similar to the engine in my 85 Fiero, anyone?<P>------------------<BR>Russ||||reg||5
Z||000001||baldlobo||09-13-2000||11:01 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rnoswal:<BR><B>There are a few postal jeeps in the junkyard around here and I was wondering if anyone knows how I can tell if they are the super duty engines. They had the carbureted intake but the carbs are gone. They are 4 cylinder and look similar to the engine in my 85 Fiero, anyone?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>SD are race engines not postal engines you'll only find them here <A HREF="http://www.gtsonline.com/krp/" TARGET=_blank>www.gtsonline.com/krp/</A>  or in the odd junked race car. oh ya one more thing look at this (under faq) site as well <A HREF="http://www.homestead.com/fiero2m4/index.html" TARGET=_blank>www.homestead.com/fiero2m4/index.html</A> it has really good Iron Duke info on it(the FAQ I mean <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<p>[This message has been edited by baldlobo (edited 09-13-2000).]||||reg||1
